\begin{theorem}\label{thm:main2} For any allowable integers $(p,q_1,q_2)$ other than $(0,0,1)$, $(0, 1, 0)$, and $(1,1,0)$  the generalized Eschenburg space $\mathcal{E}^{4n-1}_{p,q_1,q_2}$ with $n\geq 2$ has almost positive curvature with respect to Wilking's metric if and only if one of the following occurs:

\begin{itemize} \item $0, p \in [\min\{q_1+q_2,q_2\}, \max\{q_1+q_2,q_2\}]$

\item  $p\geq q_1 + q_2 > 0$ and $q_1\geq 0$

\end{itemize}

In addition, for the exceptional triples, the Wilking metric is not almost positively curved.
\end{theorem}

post_theorem_intro_text:
Based on the Jordan constant $12$ of $\mathrm{Bir}(\mathbb{P}^2, \Delta)$, we establish a Jordan constant for the three-dimensional volume-preserving Cremona group $\mathrm{Bir}(\mathbb{P}^3, \Delta)$.
\begin{theorem} \label{thmthree}
A Jordan constant for \( \mathrm{Bir}(\mathbb P^3, \Delta) \) is \( 60\).
\end{theorem}

We extend the analysis to the geometric Jordan property, which further requires the abelian normal subgroup to be embedded in an algebraic torus. We show the weak geometric Jordan property for $\mathrm{Bir}(\mathbb{P}^2)$, which allows the abelian group $A$ in each finite subgroup $G$ to be not necessarily normal.
\begin{definition}\label{def2}
A group $\mathcal{G}$ has the \emph{weak geometric Jordan property} if there exists a constant $J$ such that any finite subgroup $G \leqslant \mathcal{G}$ contains an abelian subgroup $A \leqslant G$ with index $[G:A] \leq J$, and $A$ is contained in an algebraic torus of $\mathcal{G}$.
\end{definition}

\begin{theorem} \label{thmgeo}
$\mathrm {Bir}(\mathbb P^2)$ satisfies the weak geometric Jordan property with a constant $288\cdot 16$.
\end{theorem}
In Section 2, we will review some preliminaries regarding finite subgroups of $\mathrm{Bir}(\mathbb{P}^2)$ and volume-preserving maps. In Section 3, we will derive the exact sequence as above, which reduces the task of finding a Jordan constant to enumerating certain Calabi-Yau pairs on $G$-minimal surfaces. In Section 4, we explicitly find the Jordan constant for $\mathrm{Bir}(\mathbb{P}^2, \Delta)$. In Section 5, we show that this Jordan constant is optimal and we present a way to find volume-preserving subgroups regularized on del Pezzo surfaces. In Section 6, we extend the analysis of the Jordan property to the three-dimensional volume-preserving Cremona group $
\mathrm{Bir}(\mathbb{P}^3, \Delta)$. In Section 7, we find a weak geometric Jordan constant for the plane Cremona group.
\subsection*{Acknowledgments}

I sincerely thank Joaquín Moraga for proposing this project and helpful discussions, the ideas from which essentially form the outline of the paper. Special thanks to Zhijia Zhang for valuable comments and for the idea of finding volume-preserving subgroups on del Pezzo surfaces. I am grateful to Burt Totaro for helpful conversations and comments. I also thank Ko Honda, Raphaël Rouquier, Jas Singh and José Yáñez for helpful comments.
